  ],
  "usage": "Give board, mcu_rail (a rail name or volts), five_tolerant, rails rows {name, volts, source, notes}, gpio rows {signal, pin, dir: in|out|io|od|analog|pwm, rail (empty = MCU rail), pull: none|up|down, notes} and i2c rows {bus, addr as 0x48 / 72 / 8-bit form, device, khz, notes}. It returns issues (duplicate pins or signals, I2C address conflicts and reserved addresses, 8-bit addresses converted, voltage-level mismatches, open-drain without pull-up), per-bus speed, and a C header, Markdown and JSON export. The project's saved record is read and written with MCP tool_data (tool interface-contract), the same record the app's Save button writes.",
  "sources": [
    "NXP UM10204 I2C-bus specification rev. 7: table 4 (reserved addresses), section 5 (speed modes)",
    "JEDEC JESD8C / JESD8-5: CMOS input levels VIH = 0.7 VDD, VIL = 0.3 VDD",
    "Absolute maximum VDD + 0.3 V: typical MCU datasheet rating (rule of thumb; check the part)"
  ],
  "view": true
}